A||||9||theogre||Fuel Mileage revisited.||||1||
Z||000000||theogre||06-25-2001||08:16 PM||||In another thread <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/011518.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/011518.html</A>  , well a couple others.... I mentioned not topping the tank to improve fuel mileage...<P>Ken Wittlief asked,,,<P>Say Ogre<BR>you have to explain to me?! How do you know what your MPG performance is if you dont top the tank off until it gets to the filler neck? how do you know if its a gallon from the top, or two, or a quart, or an ounce?!<P>and how do you know how full it was last time?!<P>I expect the point at which the handle kicks off the first time, the second... is very un-repeatable - so maybe you were getting better gas mileage when you didnt top it off cause you didnt really know if you were putting as much fuel in the tank as you did last time. I dont think the gas gauge is a good indicator either.<P>I have noticed when I fill the tank the gauge will point near full after I start the car - and during the next mile or so it will climb - I doubt its accurate near the top.<P>Ken, and others,<P>You have to measure over many tanks. I nearly always calc my mileage, so that means 2 years of tracking it. Too bad I didn't keep all the old records more.<P>Over time you'll see the patterns develop. One thing that helps it to use the same nozell type or better, the same pump whenever you can. These nozells are really quite predictable once you know how they work. (I had a long talk with one of our pump service people about these when I used to work at a gas station. Was very enlightening.)<P>It also helps that my driving is quite predictable most days. Same route to/from work and a couple other places.<P>Over the last 3 weeks, to keep this short, I've used 7-8 gallons a week.<P>Without stuffing the tank #'s<P>6/9 7.9 gal 26.8mpg (211.75 miles)<BR>6/17 7.006gal 28.09mpg (196.8 miles)<BR>6/25 7.219gal 27.04mpg (195.25 miles)<P>Average over 3 weeks 27.31mpg<P>When I was stuffing the tank. The best I got was 24 somethimes 25 mpg. Average was a high 23. all driving the same routes etc.<P>Without a 5th wheel and a few other things, no mileage calc is perfect but the above diferance is pretty big. And it's held up now over about 6-8 weeks. Yes, there is some diferance from week to week, but the average is holding. If the nozzels had huge drift you'd see bigger week to week changes than above. My range is staying inside 1.5 MPG error from top to bottom.<P>Will this work for everyone? maybe not. It's something to try. It certainly won't hurt to let the pump do it's job and cut off when the nozzel says full.<P>Like I said tho,,, try to use the same nozzel or preferably the same pump. In most cases, you can stay with nozzel type simply by using the same station each time. Large New stations are best. All those pumps will have new nozzels of the same kind. (Don't change fuel grades durring testing...)||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||06-25-2001||10:01 PM||||I usually "stuff the tank" so I know that it is full, and because my sender hasnt been fixed yet (have to get around to dropping that tank...), I have to rely on my trip odo for how much gas I have left.  I figure that if I'm pushing 220 miles on a tank, I better refuel.<P>And usually, I'm filling up as much as I can in case gas prices go way up.  Surprisinly, they have come down to a quite tolerable level.  I think the lowest I've seen is $1.37, which is very reasonable I've heard.  Who knows though, I might go out tomorrow and see that it jumped way up.  I better keep my mouth shut then!!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
